WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:16.370
The next morning, Peter arrived, and again the two children climbed together to the high meadows.

2
00:00:16.371 --> 00:00:23.994
The summer passed, and Heidi spent her days among the grasses and flowers with her new friends, Peter and the goats.

3
00:00:23.995 --> 00:00:28.988
When autumn came, the wind blew colder, and Heidi could no longer go up the mountain.

4
00:00:28.989 --> 00:00:31.475
Eventually, snow began to fall.

5
00:00:31.476 --> 00:00:34.833
Heidi watched the white flakes cover the mountainside.

6
00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:39.402
It was winter and too cold even for Peter to take the goats out.

7
00:00:39.403 --> 00:00:41.606
He rarely came up the mountain to visit.

8
00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:45.515
Instead, he spent his days at the little school in Dorfli.

9
00:00:45.516 --> 00:00:50.211
One evening, Peter climbed through the deep snow and knocked on Grandfather's door.

10
00:00:50.212 --> 00:00:52.095
He had a message for Heidi:

11
00:00:52.096 --> 00:00:54.826
Peter's Grannie was inviting Heidi to visit.

12
00:00:54.827 --> 00:00:57.404
She had heard about Heidi all through the summer.

13
00:00:57.405 --> 00:01:01.106
Now she missed hearing Peter's stories of their days together.

14
00:01:01.107 --> 00:01:05.576
The next day, Heidi whooshed down the snowy path on Grandfather's sled.

15
00:01:05.577 --> 00:01:10.750
When they stopped at Peter's hut, Grandfather didn't want to go inside.

16
00:01:10.751 --> 00:01:15.440
So he stayed outside and fixed the holes in the walls to keep out the wind.

17
00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.202
Heidi went inside.

18
00:01:17.203 --> 00:01:21.069
In the corner, she saw a blind woman, old and bent with age.

19
00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:25.162
She went up to her and said, "It's me, Heidi."

20
00:01:25.163 --> 00:01:27.697
Peter's Grannie felt for Heidi's hand.

21
00:01:27.698 --> 00:01:32.438
"Come here, and tell me all about yourself," she said.

22
00:01:32.439 --> 00:01:38.269
Heidi told her about her life with Grandfather and described again the summer days on the mountain.

23
00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:42.604
As she talked, a smile grew on Grannie's face.

24
00:01:42.605 --> 00:01:46.529
"It is wonderful to listen to you!" she said.

25
00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:50.220
"Come back and sit beside me whenever you can."

26
00:01:50.221 --> 00:01:57.783
And so, as the winter passed, Heidi visited Grannie whenever the snow wasn't too high or the winds too cold.

27
00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:01.613
In the spring, the village pastor came to Grandfather's hut.

28
00:02:01.614 --> 00:02:05.577
Grandfather didn't go to church and didn't like to visit the village.

29
00:02:05.578 --> 00:02:09.306
He was pretty sure that the people of Dorfli didn't like him either.

30
00:02:09.307 --> 00:02:12.577
So he was surprised to see the pastor.

31
00:02:12.578 --> 00:02:17.290
The pastor greeted Grandfather and said, "I must talk with you about Heidi.

32
00:02:17.291 --> 00:02:19.866
She should have been in school a year ago."

33
00:02:19.867 --> 00:02:24.897
"I am not planning to send her to school," said Grandfather.

34
00:02:24.898 --> 00:02:29.083
"It will only fill her head with bad ideas."

35
00:02:29.084 --> 00:02:31.128
The pastor was disappointed.

36
00:02:31.129 --> 00:02:36.543
"I was hoping that next winter you would decide to live in the village," he said.

37
00:02:36.544 --> 00:02:38.671
"It would be good for the girl."

38
00:02:38.672 --> 00:02:44.369
"You mean well, but I have made my decision," replied Grandfather.

39
00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:50.552
"Then God help you," said the pastor, and he turned sadly away.

40
00:02:50.553 --> 00:02:58.122
As the spring grew warmer, Heidi returned to the high pasture with Peter, visiting Grannie on days when the weather was cool.

41
00:02:58.123 --> 00:03:06.506
Heidi would tell her about the red glow on the mountaintops and the budding fields and flowers and how Peter looked after all the goats.

42
00:03:06.507 --> 00:03:12.025
Then one day, to their surprise, Heidi and Grandfather saw Detie climbing up the mountain path.

43
00:03:12.026 --> 00:03:16.441
Detie had met a wealthy man looking for a playmate for his crippled daughter.

44
00:03:16.442 --> 00:03:19.991
Detie had immediately thought of Heidi.

45
00:03:19.992 --> 00:03:24.431
"I am taking Heidi with me to Frankfurt," she told Grandfather.

46
00:03:24.432 --> 00:03:27.125
"You are not even sending her to school."

47
00:03:27.126 --> 00:03:30.776
"Well, go, then!" thundered Grandfather.

48
00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:34.637
But inside, he felt just a little bit sad.

49
00:03:34.638 --> 00:03:40.072
Detie gathered Heidi's bundle from the cupboard, took Heidi's hand, and quickly went down the mountain.

50
00:03:40.073 --> 00:03:45.041
When Peter's Grannie found out what had happened, she opened her window and called out,

51
00:03:45.042 --> 00:03:49.769
"Detie, Detie, do not take Heidi away!"

52
00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.634
But it was too late.

53
00:03:51.635 --> 00:03:55.974
Heidi was already gone.
